  era: "c. 300 BCE \xB7 Section 7 \xB7 Mauryan Empire \xB7 c. 321 \u2013 185 BCE"
  title: Mauryan administration
  text: The empire was ruled from Pataliputra and divided into provinces under princes. A large bureaucracy collected taxes and ran a standing army and a network of spies. Megasthenes, the Greek envoy, described the city councils of Pataliputra in his Indica.
